# The root .env targets the LIVE production database

The repo root `.env` (loaded by `apps/server/src/config.ts` and
`apps/server/prisma.config.ts`) points `DATABASE_URL` / `DIRECT_URL` at the
LIVE production database: real players, real balances, real money. Anything
that connects with it acts on production. There is no undo.

## Forbidden while the root .env (or any production URL) is in effect

Never run these, and never suggest running them, against it:

- `prisma migrate dev`, `npm run prisma:migrate:dev -w @poker/server` (creates and applies migrations, may prompt to reset)
- `prisma migrate reset`, `npm run db:reset`, `npm run prisma:reset -w @poker/server` (DROPS ALL DATA)
- `prisma db push` (applies schema changes without a reviewed migration, can drop columns)
- `prisma db seed`, `npm run db:seed`, `npm run prisma:seed -w @poker/server` (writes fake users and chips)
- `prisma migrate deploy`, `npm run db:migrate` except by the operator, following docs/DEPLOYMENT.md "Applying migrations"
- `npm run dev`, `npm run dev:server`, `npm run dev -w @poker/server` (the dev server recovers and runs live tables, deals hands and moves chips)
- `node apps/server/dist/index.js`, `npm start -w @poker/server`
- `node scripts/review-database.mjs`, any `review/**/live-*.mjs`
- `prisma studio` or any ad-hoc SQL/psql session with the production credentials

Safe: `prisma generate`, `prisma validate`, `prisma format` (no connection).

## How to work safely

- Server tests: from `apps/server`, ONLY `node test/support/run-tests.mjs <files>`; it forces a dead `DATABASE_URL` so nothing can reach production.
- Local development: use the Docker stack (`docker-compose.yml`, loopback-only, passwords required) with a separate env file, and point `apps/server/.env` at `127.0.0.1`. Never copy production values into it.
- Schema changes: write a reviewed, additive migration file; applying it to production is an operator task (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
- If you are unsure which database a command would reach, do not run it; ask.

# Supabase MCP

Before any Supabase work, read `supabase/README.md`. That folder is the inventory of what MCP can see.

- MCP is configured for project ref `tgfudufxslhrxbdxcnyl` in `.cursor/mcp.json`.
- The authenticated MCP login currently only reaches a different project (construction ERP). Do not use those tables (`employees`, `vehicles`, `attendance`, …) in poker code.
- MCP tools that write (`apply_migration`, `execute_sql` with DDL/DML, branch reset/merge) are subject to the same rules as above when the target is production.
- Do not commit service-role keys or database passwords. Publishable/anon keys belong only in env files, not in source.
